opography_derived/meg128/megc44n000hb.img","label":"https://pds-geosciences.wustl.edu/mgs/urn-nasa-pds-mgs_mola_topography_derived/meg128/megc44n000hb.lbl","credit":"NASA GSFC / MGS MOLA Science Team, PDS Geosciences Node","processing":"MEGC44N000HB v2.0. Co-registered native crop. Zero observations indicates a product-interpolated elevation. Counts are neither confidence intervals nor hazard measurements."},{"name":"MRO / CTX orbital mosaic","url":"https://planetarymaps.usgs.gov/mosaic/mars2020_trn/CTX/JEZ_ctx_B_soc_008_orthoMosaic_6m_Eqc_latTs0_lon0.tif","label":"https://doi.org/10.5066/P9GV1ND3","credit":"NASA / JPL-Caltech / MSSS / USGS Astrogeology","processing":"Mars 2020 TRN CTX 6 m orthoimage. Cropped in source EQC meters, area-averaged to 1344 by 784, valid pixels stretched at 1st and 99th percentiles. Zero source DN is nodata, masked output is transparent."},{"name":"Mars 2020 / Perseverance waypoints","url":"https://mars.nasa.gov/mmgis-maps/M20/Layers/json/M20_waypoints.json","label":"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/mars-2020-perseverance/location-map/","credit":"NASA / JPL-Caltech, Mars 2020 mission mapping team","processing":"Three end-of-drive point records selected by sol and RMC. Coordinates retained as published. Suggested walk connects snapped grid centers independently of rover history."}],"science_context":[{"sol":13,"title":"Octavia E. Butler landing","note":"The starting location anchors the plan to the crater floor where Perseverance began its investigation of Jezero.","url":"https://doi.org/10.1126/sciadv.abo4856"},{"sol":700,"title":"After the depot campaign","note":"Ten sols before this waypoint, Perseverance completed the Three Forks depot near the base of the ancient delta. The marker identifies the later rover position.","url":"https://science.nasa.gov/photojournal/perseverances-three-forks-sample-depot-map/"},{"sol":1100,"title":"Margin Unit campaign","note":"Twelve sols before this waypoint, Perseverance sealed a silica-cemented carbonate core at Bunsen Peak. The marker gives the rover position on sol 1100.","url":"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/mars-2020-perseverance/mars-rock-samples/"}],"sha256":{"jezero.json":"a1e95a431305eedcd4280d723046afeada7983ddfa7a2031e49416c63c17c335","jezero-ctx.webp":"7f1dbed9e160b317b7af470e549996e028836e144ddae648cf389d03d4974c15"},"upstream_ctx_sha256":"842b457afee7c2672022b66e3f60be836c6d52e99474015bfd9ced60099b8615"},"assumptions":["Exploratory grid model. Each cell is roughly 440 by 463 meters. Sub-cell hazards are unresolved.","Local cell grade or directional edge grade above 18% excludes travel. Diagonals cannot cross blocked corners. This threshold is a scenario assumption.","Effort is horizontal distance in km times (1 + 6 \u00d7 mean local grade), plus 10 \u00d7 positive climb in km.","Penalty per km blends normalized grade, zero-shot MOLA bins and proximity to excluded cells. Total score = effort + 4 \u00d7 integrated penalty. Scores are dimensionless planning indices.","No physiological, radiation-dose, weather, oxygen or walking-time model. The recommended path is hypothetical."]}